    "question": {
      ":question/id": "3ae06c03-f024-558d-ac17-ee26dedd2db1",
      ":question/problem": "Which of the following statements are true, given that $A$ is a $4\\times 4$ matrix and $$\n\\text{Null}(A)=\\{\\begin{bmatrix}-4{x}_{1} \\\\ 0 \\\\ 3{x}_{2} \\\\ 3{x}_{1}\\end{bmatrix}\\mid {x}_{1},{x}_{2}\\in\\mathbb{R}\\}?\n$$\n\nSelect all that apply.",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Since $A$ is a $4\\times 4$ matrix, the invertible matrix theorem states the following:\n\n$$ A\\text{ is invertible}\\quad\\Longleftrightarrow\\quad\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}\\text{Col}(A)&=\\mathbb{R}^{4} \\\\ \\text{rank}(A)&=4 \\\\ \\text{Null}(A)&=\\{0\\} \\\\ \\text{nullity}(A)&=0\\end{aligned}\\right. $$\n\nThe supplied nullspace can be written as the span of the independent vectors in\n\n$${x}_{1}\\begin{bmatrix}-4 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix} + {x}_{2}\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}$$\n\nHence $\\text{dim(Null}(A))=2$, so $A$ is not invertible.\n\nWe have $\\text{rank}(A)<4$, $\\text{nullity}(A)>0$, $\\text{Null}(A)\\ne\\{0\\}$, and $\\text{Col}(A)\\ne\\mathbb{R}^{4}$. In particular, $\\text{rank}(A)=2$ and $\\text{nullity}(A)=2$.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement $\\text{dim(Null}(A))\\ne 1$ is true. $\\text{nullity}(A)=2$.\n\n- Statement $A\\text{ is invertible}$ is false. $A$ is not invertible.\n\n- Statement $\\text{rank}(A)<4$ is true. $\\text{rank}(A)=2$; the rank counts pivot columns.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is $\\text{dim(Null}(A))\\ne 1$; $\\text{rank}(A)<4$ only.",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/moderate",
